# Emergency brake ONLY (AC4a): per-App `github_apps.review_enabled`
# (dashboard Pause/Resume) is the primary review control. This env stops ALL
# reviews platform-wide only when set to exactly "false" (case-sensitive, no
# trim). Unset / "" / "true" / "TRUE" / any other value → per-App governs.
# Leave unset.
REVIEW_ENABLED=

# Dashboard GitHub OAuth App login credentials — user-to-server,
# separate from the review GitHub App (whose Worker-env secrets were retired —
# per-App credentials now live encrypted in D1). Create the OAuth App
# (distinct from a GitHub App); its
# Authorization callback URL must be {origin}/dashboard/oauth/callback.
#
# "GITHUB_" (reserved prefix), so the GitHub-side names are
# OAUTH_CLIENT_ID / OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET (under the `staging` environment —
# Settings → Environments → staging). OAUTH_CLIENT_ID is a **variable**
# (client id is not sensitive); OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET is a **secret**. The
# Deploy workflow passes them into the Worker as GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID /
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET (the `wrangler secret bulk` JSON keys — the
# names src/worker/env.ts reads). The .dev.vars keys below keep the
# Worker-side GITHUB_ names for local wrangler dev; only the GitHub-side
# names drop the prefix.
# Set as GitHub Actions secrets (the deploy workflow injects them into the
# Worker via `wrangler secret bulk`); .dev.vars for local wrangler dev.
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Independent session-cookie HMAC key (openssl rand -base64 32). Never reuse
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET — rotation must stay decoupled.
DASHBOARD_SESSION_SECRET=

# Multi-App envelope master key: AES-256-GCM secretbox for the
# github_apps credentials stored in D1 — the App private key / webhook secret
# are encrypted with this before insert (src/dashboard/secretbox.ts). Base64
# of exactly 32 random bytes (openssl rand -base64 32). Independent of
# DASHBOARD_SESSION_SECRET — never reuse it (rotation decoupled). Missing or
# malformed → encryption-dependent dashboard routes fail closed (5xx). Set as
# GitHub Actions secrets (the deploy workflow injects them into the Worker via
# `wrangler secret bulk`); .dev.vars for local wrangler dev.
DASHBOARD_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Dashboard access control: comma-separated GitHub logins that
# are bootstrapped as `admin` at the OAuth callback when they have no users
# row yet (case-insensitive). A Worker VAR, not a secret — login names are
# public identity; set in wrangler.jsonc `vars` (or the Cloudflare dashboard's
# Worker variable settings) and redeploy; .dev.vars for local wrangler dev.
# Unset → the FIRST login against an EMPTY users table becomes admin
# (first-login fallback); every other unknown login is denied (invite-only
# 403 page, zero cookies) until an admin adds it on the Members page.
ADMIN_LOGINS=

# Provider API keys and the review model chain are NOT Worker env
# (AL-24-5 zero global fallback): configure them per App on the dashboard
# Settings page (/dashboard/apps/<slug>/settings) — keys are stored encrypted
# in D1, the chain is plaintext config. An App without the keys its chain
# needs fails its reviews closed (review_failures stage=pipeline → retry →
# DLQ). The OMP_REVIEW_MODEL / OMP_MODEL_KEY / `bun run keys` env surface was
# retired — nothing below this line ever reaches the review container.

# Ops alert webhook (architect verdict AL-6 — OPTIONAL, secret
# class): when set, the 15-min cron sweep POSTs the `ops_sweep_alert` payload
# here when review_failures over the trailing 24h exceed the threshold (JSON
# body, 3s timeout; a POST failure degrades to a warn log, never throws).
# Unset = log-only alerting. Set as a GitHub Actions secret (optional — the
# deploy workflow writes it to the Worker only when set); .dev.vars for local
# wrangler dev.
# ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# mstar-harness plugin root inside the review container (image default).
# HARNESS_PLUGIN_ROOT=/opt/mstar-harness

# Permission set for the review GitHub App (§7.6 — documentation
# only, not env keys; one fresh-App contract, no old-App migration branch).
# The Worker mints two purpose-scoped grants from the single createAppAuth
# point (src/pipeline/comment.ts), each restricted to the one repository:
#   review-write — Worker-only client; never handed to the Sandbox:
#     contents: write       ← exists for exactly one purpose: resolving
#                             positively verified, Inspector-owned review
#                             threads. No code-write, push or merge authority,
#                             and no write token ever reaches the model.
#     metadata: read
#     pull_requests: write  ← the review + its line comments
#     issues: write         ← the single overall-comment upsert
#     checks: write         ← advisory review Check Runs (execution status
#                             only; NEVER an approval or merge gate)
#   sandbox-read — every Sandbox/smoke token: contents: read, metadata: read,
#                  pull_requests: read (the shipped "gh pr diff" step runs
#                  with exactly this token, so the read grant must cover it)
# The sandbox grant is asserted against the RETURNED capabilities
# (assertSandboxGrant, spec §7.6) — contents/metadata/pull_requests read,
# every other returned permission read-only, repositorySelection "selected",
# exactly the requested repository; a broader or unscoped grant fails closed.
# The same five permissions are the fresh-App manifest
# (src/dashboard/manifest.ts `buildManifest`) this branch commits.
# Webhook events subscribed: pull_request, issue_comment
